# continuity — an action in place does not end the phase
#
# A grab in the Test Yard changes neither the area nor the hour, and brings nothing new into view, so
# its CONTINUE carries the phase on (NarrativeController.ContinueNarrationSegment): nothing greys into
# history, no observation is made, the button just tried is spent ("[no longer possible]"), and the
# keyword it came from still answers a click. Thinking about the rack again offers something other
# than the grab already offered — the proposal ledger is not cleared.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Yard" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Rack" --organs arms=2 --grant-mm woodcraft

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal grab
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
state
regions

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect SUCCESS
expect-verb grab
expect Item received:

click button
wait
advance 12 180
state
regions
# The phase carried on: no separator, no fresh observation, the grab spent.
expect-not after trying to
expect-state actions action 0 verb=grab state=spent

# The keyword still answers; another thought offers something new. Examining is pinned, with a
# means that has the Observation function, since any other refuses to examine (WillingnessRules).
goal examine
means woodcraft
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
regions
# A second button beside the spent one: the keyword answered, and the new act is live.
expect-state actions action 0 verb=grab state=spent
expect-state actions action 1 verb=examine state=live
expect-not after trying to
quit
